<title>FRANCE: New York top source for Paris air cargo imports.</title>
<headline>New York top source for Paris air cargo imports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top originating gateway for import traffic into Charles de Gaulle and Orly Airports last month despite a strong decline in tonnage.</p>
<p>The top ten airport gateways for ADP imports in November 1996 and the percentage change on November 1995 were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  New York	2,969 tonnes  down 22.7pct</p>
<p> 2  Chicago	 2,202 tonnes  down  5.8</p>
<p> 3  Hong Kong     2,176 tonnes  up    9.8</p>
<p> 4  Tokyo	   2,094 tonnes  up   36.1</p>
<p> 5  Montreal	1,594 tonnes  up   11.3</p>
<p> 6  Los Angeles   1,398 tonnes  up    6.2</p>
<p> 7  Singapore	 790 tonnes  up   58.8</p>
<p> 8  Miami	     598 tonnes  up    4.5</p>
<p> 9  Seoul	     589 tonnes  down  7.8</p>
<p> 10 Dubai	     488 tonnes  down  6.4</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
